  <section class="chapter" id="intro">
    <div class="chapter-head">
      <div class="badge">📜</div>
      <h2 data-i18n="h_1">Introduction</h2>
      <span class="idx" data-i18n="idx_1">Ch. 01</span>
    </div>
    <div data-i18n="body_1">
      <p>Questlist is a task and habit app made by <strong>Brothers Code</strong> that turns your to-dos, shopping lists and goals into missions, quests and rewards. This policy explains what information the app touches, why, and what control you have over it.</p>
      <p>By using Questlist, you agree to the practices described here. If anything is unclear, you can reach us using the contact details in Chapter 09.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter" id="data">
    <div class="chapter-head">
      <div class="badge">🗂️</div>
      <h2 data-i18n="h_2">Information We Collect</h2>
      <span class="idx" data-i18n="idx_2">Ch. 02</span>
    </div>
    <div data-i18n="body_2">
      <p>Questlist does not require an account, a sign-up, or a name. Everything you create &mdash; quests, missions, notes, your level, coins and streaks &mdash; is stored only in a local database on your own device.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Content you create:</strong> task titles, notes, checklist items, deadlines and priorities. This never leaves your device and is not sent to Brothers Code or any server we run.</li>
        <li><strong>Progress data:</strong> your level, XP, coins, streaks, unlocked skins and themes. Also stored locally only.</li>
        <li><strong>Advertising data:</strong> if you see ads in the app, our ad partner (Google AdMob) may collect device identifiers and usage data to show and measure ads. This is covered in Chapter 03.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="callout"><span class="ic">💡</span><span>Short version: your quest log is yours. We don't have a copy of it.</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter" id="ads">
    <div class="chapter-head">
      <div class="badge">📣</div>
      <h2 data-i18n="h_3">Advertising</h2>
      <span class="idx" data-i18n="idx_3">Ch. 03</span>
    </div>
    <div data-i18n="body_3">
      <p>Questlist shows ads through <strong>Google AdMob</strong> to keep the app free. AdMob and its partners may collect and use data (such as advertising identifiers and general usage information) to serve and measure ads, as described in <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
      <p>On your first launch, Questlist shows a consent form through Google's <strong>User Messaging Platform (UMP)</strong>, following the EU/UK consent framework. You choose there whether to allow personalized ads, and you can change that choice at any time from within the app.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter" id="notif">
    <div class="chapter-head">
      <div class="badge">🔔</div>
      <h2 data-i18n="h_4">Notifications</h2>
      <span class="idx" data-i18n="idx_4">Ch. 04</span>
    </div>
    <div data-i18n="body_4">
      <p>If enabled, Questlist can send a local reminder when your daily streak is about to reset. This notification is scheduled and generated entirely on your device &mdash; no notification data is sent to or processed by any external server.</p>
      <p>You can turn streak reminders on or off at any time from <strong>Profile &rarr; Settings</strong>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter" id="storage">
    <div class="chapter-head">
      <div class="badge">🔒</div>
      <h2 data-i18n="h_5">Data Storage &amp; Security</h2>
      <span class="idx" data-i18n="idx_5">Ch. 05</span>
    </div>
    <div data-i18n="body_5">
      <p>All of your quests, missions, notes and progress are stored locally on your device using Android's Room database. Brothers Code does not operate a backend or cloud service for Questlist, and we do not back up, sync or have access to your data.</p>
      <p>Because there's no account or server-side copy, uninstalling the app or clearing its storage permanently deletes your data &mdash; there is nothing on our side to remove.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter" id="children">
    <div class="chapter-head">
      <div class="badge">🧒</div>
      <h2 data-i18n="h_6">Children's Privacy</h2>
      <span class="idx" data-i18n="idx_6">Ch. 06</span>
    </div>
    <div data-i18n="body_6">
      <p>Questlist is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided us with personal information, please contact us using the details in Chapter 09 and we will take appropriate steps.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter" id="rights">
    <div class="chapter-head">
      <div class="badge">⚖️</div>
      <h2 data-i18n="h_7">Your Rights</h2>
      <span class="idx" data-i18n="idx_7">Ch. 07</span>
    </div>
    <div data-i18n="body_7">
      <p>Since Questlist stores your content locally and doesn't tie it to an identity, most data-protection rights (such as those under the GDPR) are already in your hands:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Access &amp; portability:</strong> your data is on your device at all times &mdash; there is nothing held elsewhere to request.</li>
        <li><strong>Deletion:</strong> uninstalling the app, or clearing its storage from Android settings, erases all of your in-app data immediately.</li>
        <li><strong>Advertising choices:</strong> you can review or withdraw ad-personalization consent at any time from within the app's consent settings.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter" id="changes">
    <div class="chapter-head">
      <div class="badge">🔄</div>
      <h2 data-i18n="h_8">Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <span class="idx" data-i18n="idx_8">Ch. 08</span>
    </div>
    <div data-i18n="body_8">
      <p>We may update this policy as Questlist evolves. Changes will be posted on this page with a new "last updated" date. We encourage you to review it periodically.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter" id="contact">
    <div class="chapter-head">
      <div class="badge">✉️</div>
      <h2 data-i18n="h_9">Contact</h2>
      <span class="idx" data-i18n="idx_9">Ch. 09</span>
    </div>
    <p data-i18n="contact_intro">Questions about this policy or how Questlist handles information can be sent here:</p>
    <div class="contact-card">
      <div class="contact-row">
        <div>
          <div class="label" data-i18n="label_dev">Developer</div>
          <div class="value">Brothers Code</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="contact-row">
        <div>
          <div class="label" data-i18n="label_email">Email</div>
          <div class="value" id="email-value">geral@brotherscode.pro</div>
        </div>
        <button class="copy-btn" id="copy-email" type="button" data-i18n="copy_btn">Copy</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer class="end">
    <div class="brand">Questlist</div>
    <div data-i18n="footer_built">Built by Brothers Code</div>
  </footer>
</div>

